@baseUrl=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/participants
@poolParticipantId=REPLACE_WITH_POOL_PARTICIPANT_ID
@poolId=REPLACE_WITH_POOL_ID
@addressId=REPLACE_WITH_RETAILER_OWN_ADDRESS_ID
@accessToken=REPLACE_WITH_RETAILER_ACCESS_TOKEN

# See 00-smooth-flow.http for a chained run that creates a real pool/
# address/token end to end instead of hand-editing the placeholders above.
# Note address_ref must be one of the caller's own addresses (checked
# server-side) — it can't just be any address id.

### join a pool (RETAILER only — user_ref is derived from the token, not
### sent). No payment_ref: the backend computes the contribution amount,
### creates the Payment (PENDING) and a Thawani checkout session itself,
### and returns the checkoutUrl to redirect the retailer to. The
### participant starts PENDING_PAYMENT — see payments.http for confirming
### it once the retailer pays.

POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "pool_ref": "{{poolId}}",
    "address_ref": "{{addressId}}",
    "quantity": 15
}

### list poolParticipants (ADMIN sees all; anyone else only their own)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### list poolParticipants for a given pool (ADMIN use case: see everyone in a pool)

GET {{baseUrl}}?pool_ref={{poolId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### get poolParticipant by id

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{poolParticipantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# No PATCH — quantity is no longer editable after joining (it's what the
# Thawani checkout session was priced against). Withdraw and rejoin instead.

### withdraw (RETAILER, own participant only — pool OPEN, COMPLETED, or
### CANCELLED 7+ days ago). While the pool is still OPEN this releases the
### claimed quantity and either voids a not-yet-paid Payment or requests a
### Thawani refund of an already-COMPLETED one.

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{poolParticipantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
